  m_Name: 1987 toilets
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  title: Public Toilet Flushing Mandate 1987
  info: "The law mandating the flushing of public toilets was introduced to combat
    unhygienic behavior and maintain sanitary standards in shared facilities. Enforcement
    officers conduct surprise inspections, and offenders caught leaving a toilet
    unflushed face fines of up to SGD 500. This strict policy reflects Singapore\u2019s
    commitment to cleanliness, even in private habits, and has earned the country
    its reputation as one of the world\u2019s cleanest nations."
  image: {fileID: 21300000, guid: afe917992a9df41c1aba78e5e0f08221, type: 3}
